{% from "_macros.j2" import source %}
{{ front }}

# Risk-tier self-check

Answer the questions below for the model, dataset, agent or output you are working on. The result is a suggested tier and what that tier triggers.

!!! warning "Indicative only – {{ rc.note or "draft" }}"
    The result is indicative. The responsible AI reviewer decides the tier. Questions, logic and triggers are a draft derived from the tier descriptions in {{ rc.tier_source }} and the reasons listed in {{ rc.examples_source }}.

{% if rc.questions %}
<div class="px-tool px-riskcheck" data-px-riskcheck>
<script type="application/json" data-px-data>{{ rc | json }}</script>
<form class="px-questions" onsubmit="return false">
{% for q in rc.questions %}
<fieldset class="px-question">
<legend>{{ loop.index }}. {{ q.text | e }}</legend>
{% if q.hint %}<p class="px-question__hint">{{ q.hint | e }}</p>{% endif %}
<label><input type="radio" name="{{ q.id | e }}" value="yes"> Yes</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="{{ q.id | e }}" value="no"> No</label>
</fieldset>
{% endfor %}
</form>
<div class="px-result" data-result aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
<button type="button" class="md-button" data-action="reset">Start again</button>
</div>
{% endif %}

## The tiers

| Tier | Description (from the guideline) | What it triggers (draft) |
|------|----------------------------------|--------------------------|
{% for name, t in rc.tiers.items() -%}
| **{{ name | capitalize }}** | {{ (t.description or "–") | replace("|", "\\|") }} | {{ (t.triggers | join("; ") or "–") | replace("|", "\\|") }} |
{% endfor %}

{{ source([rc.tier_source, rc.examples_source]) }}

The questions and triggers live in `docs/data/risk_check.yml`, where the RAI lead can change them without touching code.
